# Perpendicular chords in a circle of radius 6: AC^2 + BD^2 = 144. DERIVED from
# the antipode + Thales + Pythagoras (the theorem is never cited to prove itself).
O = free
A = point: dist(O,A)=6
B = point: dist(O,B)=6
C = point: dist(O,C)=6
D = point: dist(O,D)=6, perp(A,B,C,D)
prove dist(A,C)^2 + dist(B,D)^2 = 144
